    {
      "type": "practice",
      "id": 7,
      "prompt": "Given $\\vec{u} = \\langle 3, -5 \\rangle$ and $\\vec{v} = \\langle -1, 2 \\rangle$, find $\\vec{u} - \\vec{v}$.",
      "hint": "Subtract component by component: $\\langle a - c, \\, b - d \\rangle$. Watch the signs when subtracting a negative.",
      "solution": {
        "steps": [
